<title>SPAIN: Spain's Corte Ingles '95 net profit fell eight pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Corte Ingles '95 net profit fell eight pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated results for El Corte Ingles group for 1995 in billions of pesetas unless stated.</p>
<p> Net profit					30.928  vs    33.580</p>
<p> Revenues				     1,093.251  vs 1,015.566</p>
<p> Investment				     109.819  vs    57.353</p>
<p> Equity					   359.424  vs   333.349</p>
<p> Parent company net profit		   22.446  vs    24.704</p>
<p> Workforce					 51,307  vs    48,402</p>
<p>NOTE - El Corte Ingles is privately owned and is Spain's biggest retail company with 62 stores, 26 of which came from the Galerias Preciados, the competitor it acquired in November last year.</p>
</text>
